# The critical paths, as ONE definition.
#
# grep -Ei -f reads this file as a list of extended regular expressions, one per
# line, matched case-insensitively against the changed-file list — which is
# exactly how policy/wealthflow.rego classifies them (sensitive_exact plus
# sensitive_substr, compared against lower(f)).
#
# WHY IT IS A FILE. The pattern used to be inlined in fuzz-gate.yml AND listed
# in the rego, and the two copies had already drifted: the rego counted
# firestore.indexes.json as critical, the workflow's grep did not. A PR touching
# that file was therefore denied for want of `fuzz-passed` while the job that
# applies that label never even ran on it — blocked with no way to satisfy the
# rule. Two copies of a security classifier is one more than can be kept in
# step, and test/policy_gate_test.js now asserts this file and the rego agree.
#
# Lines beginning with # are comments and are stripped before use.
firestore\.rules
firebase\.json
firestore\.indexes\.json
auth
oauth
crypto
fifo-reconcile
allocator
send-otp
verify-otp
